{"result":"{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "352419841",
    "title": "Technical Solution Document (TSD) Template",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/352419841",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 2,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "> **How to use this template** Copy this page for every new TSD. Fill in each section in order. Delete the instruction callouts (the grey/amber guidance text) before submitting for review. A TSD is not approved for implementation until Section 8 (Decision Record) is signed off by the Technical Lead.\n>\n> **One TSD = one problem.** If you find yourself writing \"and also…\" in Section 1, you need a second TSD.\n\n---\n\ndocument-informationDocument Information\n----------------------------------------\n\n| Field | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Document ID** | TSD-[JIRA-KEY] |\n| **Author(s)** | [Name] — [Squad / Role] |\n| **Reviewer(s)** | [Lead name] — [Role] |\n| **Created** | [DD MMM YYYY] |\n| **Version** | v0.1 — Draft |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Related Jira** | [JIRA-KEY] |\n\n---\n\nversion-historyVersion History\n------------------------------\n\n| Version | Date | Summary of Change | Author |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| v0.1 | [DD MMM YYYY] | Initial draft | [Name] |\n\n---\n\n1-problem-statement1. Problem Statement\n---------------------------------------\n\n> ℹ **Guidance:** State the problem in 3–5 sentences. This is **not the solution**. Do not mention technology choices here. A reader who knows nothing about this ticket should understand exactly what is broken or missing after reading this section.\n>\n> ⚠ **Do NOT include:** options, implementation details, or the recommended approach. Those belong in later sections.\n\n### 11-context1.1 Context\n\n[Describe the business or technical context in 2–3 sentences. What feature or flow does this affect?]\n\n### 12-problem1.2 Problem\n\n[What specifically is broken, missing, or needs to change? Be precise. Avoid vague language like \"improve\" or \"enhance\".]\n\n### 13-impact-if-not-solved1.3 Impact if Not Solved\n\n[What happens if we do nothing? This can be a user impact, a technical risk, a delivery risk, or a commercial consequence.]\n\n### 14-success-criteria1.4 Success Criteria\n\n[How will we know the problem is solved? State 2–4 measurable or testable outcomes.]\n\n*Example: \"User can add a product to wishlist without being logged in, and the item persists after login.\"*\n\n---\n\n2-constraints--assumptions2. Constraints & Assumptions\n------------------------------------------------------\n\n> ℹ **Guidance:** Constraints are non-negotiable boundaries. Assumptions are things you are treating as true for the purpose of this document. Both must be listed **before** the options analysis — they are what the options are evaluated against.\n>\n> ⚠ If an assumption turns out to be wrong, the TSD must be updated and re-reviewed. Do not proceed to implementation if a constraint has changed.\n\n### 21-constraints2.1 Constraints\n\n| Constraint | Detail |\n| --- | --- |\n| Platform | SFCC B2C Commerce + PWA Kit on MRT. No alternative platform is in scope. |\n| Integration layer | All backend system calls must route through MuleSoft. No new direct point-to-point connections from SFCC. |\n| Storefront scope | Solution must work across all 7 storefronts (AU, UK, US Dom, US Intl, EU, ME). No single-market workarounds. |\n| [Add constraint] | [Detail] |\n\n### 22-assumptions2.2 Assumptions\n\n| Assumption | Risk if Wrong |\n| --- | --- |\n| [State assumption] | [What breaks if this is not true?] |\n| [State assumption] | [What breaks if this is not true?] |\n\n---\n\n3-options-analysis3. Options Analysis\n-------------------------------------\n\n> ℹ **Guidance:** List every viable approach considered — including \"do nothing\" if relevant. Keep descriptions short (2–4 sentences per option). Pros and cons should be **specific to this problem and these constraints** — not generic.\n>\n> ⚠ **Do NOT include implementation steps in this section.** Save implementation detail for Section 5 (the chosen option only). Options you discarded still need a brief entry so reviewers can see you considered them.\n\n### 31-options-summary3.1 Options Summary\n\n| Option | Pros | Cons | Viable? |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Option A** — [Short name] | + [Specific advantage] + [Specific advantage] | - [Specific disadvantage] - [Specific disadvantage] | Yes |\n| **Option B** — [Short name] | + [Specific advantage] | - [Specific disadvantage] | Yes |\n| **Option C** — [Short name] | + [Specific advantage] | - [Disqualifying reason — be specific] | No |\n\n### 32-option-detail3.2 Option Detail\n\n> ℹ For each viable option, write 2–4 sentences of detail. Do not write implementation steps. Focus on how the option fits (or conflicts with) the constraints in Section 2.\n\n#### option-a--short-nameOption A — [Short name]\n\n[Describe the approach in 2–4 sentences. What pattern or mechanism does it use? Why is it viable against the constraints?]\n\n#### option-b--short-nameOption B — [Short name]\n\n[Describe the approach in 2–4 sentences.]\n\n#### option-c--short-name-discardedOption C — [Short name] *(Discarded)*\n\n[One sentence on why this was discarded. Example: \"Discarded — requires a direct SFCC-to-AP21 connection, which violates the MuleSoft constraint.\"]\n\n---\n\n4-recommended-option--rationale4. Recommended Option & Rationale\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n> ℹ **Guidance:** State which option you are recommending and why. This should be 1–2 short paragraphs. Reference the constraints and success criteria from Sections 1 and 2. Do **not** repeat the full option description — just the reason for the choice.\n>\n> ⚠ If there is genuine disagreement between the author and reviewer about which option to choose, do not resolve it here. Escalate to the Lead and document the outcome in the Decision Record (Section 8).\n\n### 41-recommended-option4.1 Recommended Option\n\n**[Option X — Short name]**\n\n### 42-rationale4.2 Rationale\n\n[Why this option over the others? Be specific. Example: \"Option A is recommended over Option B because it reuses the existing MuleSoft order event pattern, which ke