      "value": "Document Information\n--------------------\n\n| Field | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Document ID** | TSD-SFCC-303 |\n| **Author(s)** | Victor T. Crisostomo — Technical Architect / Squad A |\n| **Reviewer(s)** | [Lead name] — Technical Lead |\n| **Created** | 12 Aug 2026 |\n| **Version** | v0.1 — Draft |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Related Jira** | SFCC-303 |\n\n---\n\nVersion History\n---------------\n\n| Version | Date | Summary of Change | Author |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| v0.1 | 12 Aug 2026 | Initial draft | Victor T. Crisostomo |\n\n---\n\n1. Problem Statement\n--------------------\n\n### 1.1 Context\n\nThe Zimmermann storefront serves a VIC (Very Important Customer) segment that has access to exclusive products not available to general customers. Currently, SFCC has no native mechanism to restrict product visibility at the customer group level — all products are visible to all users regardless of segment.\n\n### 1.2 Problem\n\nSite Merchandisers have no way to flag a product as VIC-exclusive in Business Manager. Without this, VIC-exclusive products are either exposed to all customers (a brand and commercial risk) or must be withheld from the catalogue entirely (a merchandising limitation). There is no per-product visibility gate tied to customer group membership.\n\n### 1.3 Impact if Not Solved\n\nVIC-exclusive products cannot be listed on the storefront without being visible to all customers, undermining the exclusivity proposition for the VIC segment and potentially damaging the brand relationship with VIC customers.\n\n### 1.4 Success Criteria\n\n* A VIC-exclusive product does not appear in search results for non-VIC customers.\n* A VIC-exclusive product does not appear in category browsing for non-VIC customers.\n* A non-VIC customer navigating directly to a VIC-exclusive PDP URL receives a 404 response.\n* A VIC customer can search, browse, and view VIC-exclusive products without restriction.\n* A Site Merchandiser can set the VIC-excl